---
/**
 * Privacy — deliberately two separate stories: this website (which collects nothing) and the
 * product (which handles real financial data under a contract).
 *
 * NOT LEGALLY REVIEWED. It is factually accurate about what the site does, and it says plainly
 * that the product's binding policy is not published yet rather than inventing one. `index={false}`
 * keeps a placeholder out of search until counsel has seen it.
 */
import { url } from '@/lib/url'
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro'
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '@/consts'

const lastUpdated = 'August 2026'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this website collects (nothing) and how the product handles financial data."
  index={false}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="This website collects nothing. The product is a separate story, told separately."
    lede="Most privacy pages are long because the site behind them is doing a lot. This one is short for the opposite reason."
  />

  <section class="section-y">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="border-hairline bg-surface rounded-md mb-14 max-w-3xl border p-6">
        <p class="text-exception text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.08em] uppercase">Pre-launch notice</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          Verity is pre-launch. This page is an accurate plain-language description of what we do
          today; it is <span class="text-ink">not</span> a legal agreement and has not been reviewed
          by counsel. The binding privacy terms for the product are provided contractually to design
          partners. If you need them before then, ask.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-14">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium">This website</h2>
          <ul class="text-ink-muted mt-6 space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">
            <li>
              <span class="text-ink">No forms.</span> There is nowhere on this site to submit
              anything, so there is nothing for us to store.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-ink">No analytics and no tracking pixels.</span> We do not know who
              you are, which pages you read, or where you came from.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-ink">No cookies</span>, which is why there is no cookie banner. There
              is nothing to consent to.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-ink">No third-party requests.</span> Fonts are self-hosted; there is
              no CDN, no embedded video, and no chat widget. Reading this page contacts our server
              and nothing else.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-ink-muted mt-6 leading-relaxed">
            Our host keeps ordinary server logs (IP address, request time, page requested) for
            operational and security purposes. If we later add privacy-preserving, cookie-free
            analytics, this page will say so before it is switched on.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium">The product</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-muted mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
            The product is a different matter: it necessarily handles your financial data. How that
            works in practice is described in detail on the
            <a href={url("/security")} class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">security page</a>,
            and summarised here.
          </p>
          <ul class="text-ink-muted mt-6 space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">
            <li>
              <span class="text-ink">What we hold:</span> bank transactions retrieved through your
              Plaid connection, invoices read from your billing system, and the credit notes and
              audit records Verity itself creates.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-ink">What we do not hold:</span> your banking or accounting
              passwords. Bank access runs through Plaid's consent flow; billing access through your
              provider's sign-in-and-approve screen, which returns a scoped token. There is no field
              anywhere in the product for pasting a credential.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-ink">Isolation:</span> every row is scoped to your organisation and
              enforced by the database, not by application code remembering to filter.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-ink">Purpose:</span> your data is used to operate the service for
              you. We do not sell it, and we do not use it to train models for anyone else.
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="text-ink">Sub-processors:</span> our hosting provider, Plaid for bank
              connectivity, and the model provider used for advisory narration parsing. A current
              list is provided to design partners and will be published here at launch.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium">Getting your data out, or deleted</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-muted mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
            Design partner agreements cover export and deletion. In practice: you can disconnect a
            feed at any time from the product, and a written deletion request reaches a person who
            can action it. Audit records for credits already issued are retained for the period your
            agreement specifies, because a financial audit trail that can be deleted on request is
            not an audit trail.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium">Contact</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-muted mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
            Privacy questions go to
            <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4">
              {CONTACT_EMAIL}
            </a> and reach the people who built the system, not a ticket queue.
          </p>
          <p class="text-ink-subtle mt-8 text-xs">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
